github.com/users/dezren39/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"author_association":"MEMBER","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"status":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"Found by the orchestration-pass weekly triage retrospective (2026-11-02, run orch-2026-11-02T22:13:54Z).\n\nEvidence: via the laptop route, `curl -s \"http://127.0.0.1:4870/api/actions.json?state=all\"` returned `{\"actions\": [], \"pending\": {...0}}`, while the aggregator store file `~/pm-stack/aggregator/actions.json` on the same host holds 13 actions (all state=applied, created 2026-10-27). The `?state=new` query correctly returns 0 pending — the bug is specific to non-new/all reads.\n\nImpact: any consumer auditing past dashboard actions (the weekly triage retrospective, code#1455, reviews ALL of Drew's dashboard actions since the last retrospective across every kind and outcome) reads a false zero from the API and can only get the truth by reading the store file directly.\n\nAcceptance: /api/actions.json supports a state filter that returns applied/rejected history (or an explicit all-history route), with a regression test pinning that a store with applied actions returns them.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- `/api/actions.json` supports a state filter that returns applied/rejected history (or an explicit all-history route exists).\n- A regression test pins that a store containing applied actions returns them from the API.\n- `?state=new` behaviour is unchanged.\n","closed_by":{"login":"dezren39","id":11225574,"node_id":"